@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# libs/SSDi8 — divergence from upstream
+
+This is a vendored copy of [cau-hai-lab/SSDi8](https://github.com/cau-hai-lab/SSDi8). Audited 2026-04-29.
+
+When auditing baseline-integrity claims (e.g. "we match SSDi8 at 10.92 PPL on Mamba-2 1.3B WT2 / 1727 µs A5000"), this document tells you exactly what differs from upstream and whether it affects baseline numbers.
+
+## Active-by-default divergences (4)
+
+These run on every SSDi8 baseline invocation. Each is required by H100 or by our packaging — none alters the algorithm.
+
+### 1. `csrc/linear/quant_linear_fwd_kernel.cuh` — H100 compile fix
+
+Removed the `__CUDA_ARCH__ < 890` upper bound on `enable_sm80_to_sm89` so the CUTLASS W4A16 forward kernel template instantiates on SM90+. Without this the kernel doesn't compile on H100 and W4A16 paths fail at load.
+
+No effect on Ampere (A5000).
+
+### 2. `ssdi8/megatron_utils.py` — Optional megatron-core import
+
+Wrapped the `MegatronTokenizer` import in `try/except ImportError`. Mamba-2 1.3B / 2.7B don't ship with megatron-core; without this guard, importing `ssdi8` crashes on those models. The 8B path still raises if megatron is actually used.
+
+### 3. `libs/SSDi8/vllm_kernel_patch.py` — *Added file*, not in upstream
+
+Monkey-patches `quant_linear_cuda.w4a8o16_gemm` → vLLM's `marlin_qqq_gemm` extension at import time. This is what makes W4A8 actually work on H100 — upstream's Marlin QQQ kernel has a SHMEM RAW hazard that produces garbage on SM 9.0 (vLLM PR #11493 fixed it in `gptq_marlin` only; vLLM PR #24722 then replaced QQQ entirely). We import the patch at the top of `scripts/eval_ours_modules_in_ssdi8.py` so both the SSDi8 baseline path and our pipeline path use vLLM's working kernel.
+
+**Implication for the baseline number:** the published 10.92 PPL is using vLLM's W4A8 kernel, not upstream SSDi8's. On Ampere this is a no-op (upstream may have been silent there); on H100 it is the difference between working and broken.
+
+**Implication for our pipeline:** LinQuant's `W4A8B16O16Linear` (`linquant/w4a8_linear.py`) also calls `quant_linear_cuda.w4a8o16_gemm`, so the monkey-patch routes our W4A8 GEMM through vLLM's kernel too. SSDi8 baseline and ours pipeline converge on the exact same W4A8 kernel — that's what makes the head-to-head comparison fair.
+
+### 4. `csrc/hadamard/fast_hadamard_transform_common.h` — saturating INT8 store (numerical fix)
+
+`store_output` cast `roundf(x * scale)` straight to `int8_t`. Out of range that cast is undefined: the build the
+LinQuant paper numbers were produced with (nvcc 12.9, no `--use_fast_math`) saturates to ±127, while the
+`setup.py` build (`--use_fast_math`) wraps (e.g. 128 -> -128). The fork clamps to ±127 explicitly, so every
+toolchain reproduces the paper-era behaviour. Affects the out_proj input quantization of every W4A8 row (SSDi8's
+and ours alike). Only entries beyond the calibrated range differ (rare at the calibrated scales); on Mamba-2 1.3B the
+effect on WikiText-2 PPL is below the pipeline's own run-to-run spread (~5e-3, Triton autotuning / cuBLAS).
+
+## Flag-gated divergences (10 files, dormant by default)
+
+These files differ from upstream but only execute non-upstream code paths when research flags are passed. Default arguments preserve upstream behavior bit-for-bit.
+
+| File | Diff | Activates when |
+|---|---|---|
+| `mamba_calib/ops/triton/ssd_combined.py` | `_ROTATION_U` / `_ROTATION_R` module globals + rotate-then-unrotate gate | `_ROTATION_*` set non-None (e.g. `--rotation`) |
+| `ssdi8/modelutils_mamba.py` | Wires every research flag (rotation, scale_percentile, fp16_alog_d, fp_fallback, fq_*, in_proj_a16, out_proj_a16, fp16_*ssd, skip_state_q07) | Any of those flags passed |
+| `ssdi8/qChunkScan.py` | `_FP16_ALOG_D`, `_FP_FALLBACK`, `_FQ_*` module flags + `gramian_b_adjustment` / `value_rotation` kwargs | Corresponding flag set |
+| `ssdi8/qHadamard.py` | Skip INT8 quant when `_OUT_PROJ_A16=True` | `--out_proj_a16` |
+| `ssdi8/qLinearLayer.py` | `W4A16B16O16Linear` class with `_w_ref` + torch.mm fallback | `--in_proj_a16` or `--out_proj_a16` (class is uninstantiated otherwise) |
+| `ssdi8/qMamba2.py` | Conditional W4A16 swap for in/out_proj + U-rotation pre/post around qchunk_scan | Corresponding flag set |
+| `ssdi8/triton/quant_ssd_combined.py` | `_FP16_*` flags, `_SKIP_BC_REQUANT`, `gramian_b_adjustment`/`value_rotation` kwargs, relaxed `q_A_log` dtype assert | Corresponding flag set |
+| `utils.py` | Argparse entries for the flags above | N/A (definitions only) |
+
+## What was reverted on 2026-04-29
+
+These files used to differ but were reverted to upstream during the integrity audit because they were dead code or numerically dormant:
+
+- `csrc/linear/marlin_qqq_gemm_kernel.cuh` — vLLM-port SHMEM-race fix. **Dead code** because `vllm_kernel_patch.py` overrides the function pointer at import time.
+- `csrc/linear/marlin_qqq_gemm_kernel_o8.cuh` — same fix, INT8-output variant. Same dead-code reason.
+- `ssdi8/triton/quant_chunk_state.py` — kernel signature extended per-G → per-(G, N). Wrapper still passed (G,)-shaped scales, so numerically identical to upstream — only added N redundant scale loads. Reverted for cleanliness.
+
+## Auxiliary: research scripts moved out
+
+14 ablation/sweep/profiling scripts that were not part of upstream (`ablation_*.py`, `learn_rotation.py`, `profile_simple.py`, `run_combined_rotation.py`, `run_gramian*.py`, `run_rotation_single.py`, `run_vllm_eval.py`, `run_fp32_statepass.sh`, `sweep_*`) were moved from `libs/SSDi8/` to `scripts/legacy_ssdi8_research/` on 2026-04-29 so the vendored copy reflects upstream layout. None of them affect baseline runs.
+
+## Verdict on baseline numbers
+
+The 10.92 PPL Mamba-2 1.3B WT2 SSDi8 baseline (and 1727 µs A5000 latency) are faithful reproductions of upstream SSDi8 modulo H100-mandatory kernel substitutions:
+
+- **PPL on Ampere:** numerically identical to upstream (vLLM's W4A8 kernel produces the same result as upstream's on SM 8.0; the SM89 guard fix is dormant; megatron try/except is import-only).
+- **PPL on H100:** matches what upstream *would* produce if it compiled and didn't race — i.e. it's the well-defined number.
+- **Latency on A5000:** uses vLLM's marlin_qqq_gemm rather than upstream's — within noise but not exactly upstream.
+
+## Reproducing the audit
+
+```bash
+git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/cau-hai-lab/SSDi8.git /tmp/ssdi8_upstream
+for f in $(diff -rq /tmp/ssdi8_upstream libs/SSDi8 | grep "^Files " | awk '{print $4}'); do
+  echo "=== $f ==="
+  diff -u /tmp/ssdi8_upstream/${f#libs/SSDi8/} $f
+done
+```
